<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lothair III, Holy Roman Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1075–1137</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Lothair of Supplinburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-i">Lothair</a> III, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a>, was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-of-saxony">Duke of Saxony</a> from 1106, King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> from 1125 and emperor from 1133. As duke he granted Holstein and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stormarn">Stormarn</a> to Adolf I of Schauenburg in 1111 and encouraged expansion against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a> east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a>. His alliance with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-welf">Welfs</a> shaped German politics after his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lothair-iii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="Lothair III, Holy Roman Emperor" width="267" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lothair_II,_Holy_Roman_Emperor.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
